    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `label_ticket` in `app/labeler.py`. `pytest -q` passes, but the only existing test checks that `LABELS` is lowercase, so nothing actually runs `label_ticket`. I tried a quick check with a fake client, but the permission settings blocked the inline script, so the function's behaviour hasn't been tested.\n\nWhat it does:\n- Sends one `client.messages.create` request to `MODEL` (`claude-sonnet-4-6`) with `max_tokens=5` and `temperature=0`.\n- The system prompt says: *\"Classify the support ticket. Answer with exactly one word from: bug, feature, question.\"* The list comes from `LABELS`, so it stays in sync if the labels change.\n- The ticket text is sent as the user message.\n- It joins the text blocks of the reply, then strips and lower-cases the result. If that isn't one of `LABELS`, it returns `\"question\"`.\n\n`claude-sonnet-4-6` accepts `temperature`, so the request is valid. Newer models (Opus 4.7 and later, Sonnet 5, Fable) reject `temperature` with a 400 error. If `MODEL` is ever changed to one of those, this call will fail.\n\nNo dependencies were added. If you want this covered by the test suite, I can add a test that uses a fake client."
  },
